1144
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:15,040
Mathematically this looks like gamma of

1145
00:43:11,599 --> 00:43:18,079
delta l= 2 * i * the integral of s of

1146
00:43:15,040 --> 00:43:20,960
new * cosine of 2<unk> delta l new d

1147
00:43:18,079 --> 00:43:22,800
new. Here s of nu represents the power

1148
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:24,640
spectrum of the light source describing

1149
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:26,400
how much energy each frequency

1150
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:28,319
contributes.

1151
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:30,160
Now if this looks familiar it should

1152
00:43:28,319 --> 00:43:32,319
because this integral is nothing but a

1153
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:34,160
fier transform.

1154
00:43:32,319 --> 00:43:36,560
You might remember that in a standard

1155
00:43:34,160 --> 00:43:39,280
