1185
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:45,520
matched within that coherence length.

1186
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:47,839
Now, think about how we use that in

1187
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:49,680
imaging. As the movable mirror scans

1188
00:44:47,839 --> 00:44:51,920
back and forth, you collect this varying

1189
00:44:49,680 --> 00:44:53,839
signal over time. Some parts of the

1190
00:44:51,920 --> 00:44:55,599
sample are closer, some are deeper, so

1191
00:44:53,839 --> 00:44:58,079
their reflected signals arrive at

1192
00:44:55,599 --> 00:44:59,680
slightly different delays.

1193
00:44:58,079 --> 00:45:01,280
When you record and reconstruct all

1194
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:03,440
those depth dependent interference

1195
00:45:01,280 --> 00:45:06,400
signals, you essentially form an image

1196
00:45:03,440 --> 00:45:08,160
one line of depth at a time. And by

1197
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:10,640
stacking those lines together, you can

1198
00:45:08,160 --> 00:45:12,319
