1216
00:45:49,520 --> 00:45:54,079
The optical path length difference is

1217
00:45:51,359 --> 00:45:57,119
given by delta L= 2 * the difference

1218
00:45:54,079 --> 00:45:58,720
between L2 and L1.

1219
00:45:57,119 --> 00:46:02,880
The phase difference between the two

1220
00:45:58,720 --> 00:46:04,640
beams is 5 = 2 pi delta L / lambda. And

1221
00:46:02,880 --> 00:46:08,880
the detected intensity at the photo

1222
00:46:04,640 --> 00:46:14,400
detector is given by I= I 1 + I2 + 2 *

1223
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:16,319
the<unk> of I 1 * I2 * cosine 5.

1224
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:17,839
Now if the two beams arrive in phase

1225
00:46:16,319 --> 00:46:19,599
meaning the optical path difference is

1226
00:46:17,839 --> 00:46:21,680
an integer multiple of the wavelength

1227
00:46:19,599 --> 00:46:23,920
that gives constructive interference

1228
00:46:21,680 --> 00:46:25,920
maximum brightness.

1229
00:46:23,920 --> 00:46:31,359
Mathematically that happens when 2 pi

1230
00:46:25,920 --> 00:46:35,359
deltal / lambda= 2 mpi or simply deltal

1231
00:46:31,359 --> 00:46:38,480
m lambda where m is an integer 0 1 2 and

1232
00:46:35,359 --> 00:46:40,720
so on. But if the path difference equals

1233
00:46:38,480 --> 00:46:43,680
an odd multiple of half wavelengths like

1234
00:46:40,720 --> 00:46:45,599
delta L= M plus 1/2* lambda then the

1235
00:46:43,680 --> 00:46:47,359
