1287
00:48:32,720 --> 00:48:36,800
columnation lens to make the light

1288
00:48:34,240 --> 00:48:38,400
travel in a parallel direction. Then it

1289
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:41,599
reaches the beam splitter where the

1290
00:48:38,400 --> 00:48:43,280
light is divided into two parts.

1291
00:48:41,599 --> 00:48:44,960
One part of the beam goes upward toward

1292
00:48:43,280 --> 00:48:47,040
the reference mirror and the other part

1293
00:48:44,960 --> 00:48:48,640
travels sideways toward the sample under

1294
00:48:47,040 --> 00:48:50,400
test.

1295
00:48:48,640 --> 00:48:52,400
The light going to the reference mirror

1296
00:48:50,400 --> 00:48:54,880
bounces back after reflection and

1297
00:48:52,400 --> 00:48:56,559
returns to the beam splitter.

1298
00:48:54,880 --> 00:48:59,200
Meanwhile, the light that goes toward

1299
00:48:56,559 --> 00:49:01,359
the sample also gets reflected, but from

1300
00:48:59,200 --> 00:49:03,280
within the tissue itself. Think of this

1301
00:49:01,359 --> 00:49:05,200
