1329
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:08,160
When you move the beam laterally across

1330
00:50:05,359 --> 00:50:10,480
the sample, for example, in the X or Y

1331
00:50:08,160 --> 00:50:12,160
direction, you collect many A scans side

1332
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:14,400
by side, building up a full

1333
00:50:12,160 --> 00:50:16,480
cross-sectional image.

1334
00:50:14,400 --> 00:50:18,720
That's the essential idea of optical

1335
00:50:16,480 --> 00:50:20,480
coherence tomography. Measuring optical

1336
00:50:18,720 --> 00:50:22,240
interference point by point and

1337
00:50:20,480 --> 00:50:26,520
reconstructing the internal micro

1338
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:26,520
structure of a sample in depth.

1339
00:50:27,680 --> 00:50:32,319
Now let's look at one of the most common

1340
00:50:29,440 --> 00:50:35,119
